      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "thm-qftx-gaga-analytic-projective-dolbeault-scalar-cohomology-1-1",
          "claim": "If $r=0$, then $X$ is a point, so a sheaf on $X$ is just its group of sections, global sections is exact, and every positive sheaf-cohomology group vanishes. The degree-zero Dolbeault complex is the identity on the fiber $E$, so the comparison is the identity by the derived-global-sections definition [F8]. Assume now $r\\ge1$. On a coordinate polydisc with holomorphic frame $s_1,\\ldots,s_n$ of $E$, write an $E$-valued form as $\\sum_{a=1}^n\\alpha_a\\otimes s_a$ and define $\\bar\\partial_E(\\sum_a\\alpha_a\\otimes s_a)=\\sum_a\\bar\\partial\\alpha_a\\otimes s_a$. If the frame changes by a holomorphic matrix $G$, then $\\bar\\partial(G\\alpha)=(\\bar\\partial G)\\wedge\\alpha+G\\bar\\partial\\alpha=G\\bar\\partial\\alpha$ because every entry of $G$ is holomorphic and hence satisfies the Cauchy–Riemann equations [F5]. Thus the local operators agree on overlaps; by [F3], their square is zero.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "A1",
            "F1",
            "F2",
            "F3",
            "F5",
            "F8",
            "given",
            "construct",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-qftx-gaga-analytic-projective-dolbeault-scalar-cohomology-2-1",
          "claim": "In a holomorphic frame, under full AC [A1], the local Dolbeault lemma [F4] applies componentwise to every closed form of positive antiholomorphic degree and gives exactness at that degree on a neighborhood of each point. At degree zero, a smooth coefficient killed by $\\bar\\partial$ satisfies the coordinate Cauchy–Riemann equations, so [F5] makes it holomorphic. Consequently the sheaf resolution $0\\longrightarrow\\mathcal O(E)\\longrightarrow\\mathcal A^{0,0}(E) \\xrightarrow{\\bar\\partial_E}\\cdots\\xrightarrow{\\bar\\partial_E} \\mathcal A^{0,r}(E)\\longrightarrow0$ is exact: its degree-zero kernel is exactly the holomorphic-section sheaf, and every positive-degree kernel is locally the preceding image.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "A1",
            "F2",
            "F4",
            "F5",
            "step 1.1",
            "construct"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-qftx-gaga-analytic-projective-dolbeault-scalar-cohomology-3-1",
          "claim": "Each $\\mathcal A^{0,j}(E)$ is a sheaf of modules over smooth functions, by pointwise scalar multiplication; hence it is $\\Gamma(X,-)$-acyclic by [F6] under [A1].",
          "step": "3.1",
          "inputs": [
            "A1",
            "F6",
            "step 2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-qftx-gaga-analytic-projective-dolbeault-scalar-cohomology-4-1",
          "claim": "Every cycle in the exact resolution of step 2.1 is an abelian sheaf on $X$, so it lies in the all-abelian-sheaves domain of the injective-resolution datum in [F8]. By [F9], full AC [A1] supplies the DC required by the acyclic-resolution theorem [F7]. Applying [F7] to that resolution and the global-sections functor gives, canonically, $H^q(X,\\mathcal O(E))\\cong H^q(\\Gamma(X,\\mathcal A^{0,\\bullet}(E)))=H^q_{\\bar\\partial}(X,E)$ for every $q\\ge0$.",
          "step": "4.1",
          "inputs": [
            "A1",
            "F7",
            "F8",
            "F9",
            "step 2.1",
            "step 3.1",
            "given"
          ]
        },
