        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "lem-qftx-gaga-projective-cover-laurent-cohomology",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "each section on $U_I$, in a standard local frame, has a unique normally convergent mixed Laurent–Taylor expansion indexed by exponent tuples $m=(m_0,\\ldots,m_r)\\in\\mathbb Z^{r+1}$ with $\\sum_i m_i=k$; its coefficient occurs on $U_I$ exactly when $N(m):=\\{i:m_i<0\\}\\subseteq I$. Restrictions preserve each coefficient. In the ordered-cover Čech complex, every mode with nonempty proper $N(m)$ has the cochain contraction, for $c\\in C^p$ and an output index $I$ of size $p$, given by $(h_mc)_I=0$ if $j\\in I$ and $(h_mc)_I=(-1)^{\\#\\{i\\in I:i<j\\}}c_{I\\cup\\{j\\}}$ if $j\\notin I$, where $j$ is the least index outside $N(m)$; the resulting subseries converge locally uniformly on the output intersections. The fixed-cover Čech cohomology is canonically the analytic sheaf cohomology whenever that cover is acyclic for the coefficient sheaf.",
          "uses": [
