          "id": "ex-qftx-gaga-analytic-untwisted-obstruction-5-1",
          "claim": "By [F2], each fiber $\\mathcal O(-1)_p$ is a one-dimensional complex vector space. Evaluation at any $p\\in X$ is the zero map from $H^0(X,\\mathcal O(-1))=0$ to this nonzero fiber, so it is not onto. This violates the defining fiberwise condition for global generation, proving that $\\mathcal O(-1)$ is not globally generated.",
          "step": "5.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F2",
            "step 1.1",
            "def. global generation"
          ]
        }
